description:
Build `AvlSet`, a self-balancing binary search tree of distinct `int`s:

```cpp
class AvlSet
{
public:
    bool insert(int key);
    bool erase(int key);
    bool contains(int key) const;
    std::size_t size() const;
    int height() const;                 // -1 when empty
    std::vector<int> toVector() const;  // in order
    bool isValid() const;               // checks the BST order, every stored height and every balance factor
};
```

- Each node stores its height. After every insert or erase, update heights and rebalance the nodes on the path back to the root with the four rotation cases (lesson 4.03).
- `isValid` recomputes everything from scratch: keys in order, stored heights correct, every balance factor in {−1, 0, +1}. The tests call it after many operations.
- The tests insert 100,000 keys in **sorted** order (a plain BST would have height 99,999) and expect the height to stay within the AVL bound.

